  "definition": "Cardiovascular disease is a major group of medical disorders that is a leading cause of death worldwide and is often identified using electrocardiograms along with clinical information such as age, gender, and weight. In this source, it is discussed as a classification category that includes groups such as myocardial infarction, ST-T segment changes, conduction disturbance, and hypertrophy.",
